# Packages for the Arch userland at /opt/arch, installed with pacman inside it
# (setup.sh) the way Omarchy's bin/omarchy-pkg-install does.
#
# Sourced from the Omarchy repo's install/omarchy-base.packages. Dropped from
# that manifest: hardware and host-only packages (bluez*, cups*, bolt,
# brightnessctl, ddcutil, asdcontrol, gpu-screen-recorder, kernel-modules-hook,
# docker*, snapper, power-profiles-daemon, printer/scanner stacks, sddm) and
# the OPR/AUR desktop apps that have no meaning without a human at the
# keyboard (aether, herdr, cliamp, localsend, …). Add AUR packages with
# `arch-run 'yay -S --noconfirm <pkg>'` (the helper
# bin/omarchy-pkg-aur-install uses) if a future skill needs one, then add them
# here.
#
# The Zap runtime itself runs on the host side of the box, from the shared
# baseline, so this list is the desktop and Arch tooling — not a second runtime.

# ── desktop: the Omarchy Hyprland session the agent drives ──────────────
hyprland
hyprland-guiutils
hyprpicker
xorg-xwayland
uwsm
wl-clipboard
foot
grim
slurp
libnotify
mako
swaybg
waybar
polkit-gnome
gnome-keyring
libsecret
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
qt5-wayland
qt6-wayland
gtk3
gtk4
adwaita-icon-theme
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
noto-fonts-cjk

# ── browser: the agent's own browser (browser lane) ─────────────────────
chromium
nss
alsa-lib
libxss
mesa

# ── base runtime inside the Arch root ───────────────────────────────────
python
python-pip
python-yaml
git
curl
wget
jq
openssl
unzip
zip
rsync
sudo
which
inetutils

# ── desktop automation on this display ──────────────────────────────────
xdotool
xorg-xrandr

# ── Arch-side tooling the agent reaches through `arch-run` ──────────────
ripgrep
fd
fzf
bat
eza
ffmpeg
imagemagick
libvips
poppler
tesseract
tesseract-data-eng
